      "writtenOn": "2022-09-16T16:40:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looked at all usages of BT_STATUS_BUSY, all look retryable except 2 places:\n\n* http://osscs/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_hd.cc;l\u003d396;drc\u003d6bf723485473ac53ba78aac3fd12482d4457c3cd\n* http://osscs/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_hf.cc;l\u003d661;drc\u003d6bf723485473ac53ba78aac3fd12482d4457c3cd\n\nBoth of which should be BT_STATUS_DONE, can be interpreted generally as: I can\u0027t do the request because it\u0027s already done, so you can assume success unless you really need to redo the request.\n\nHow about I file a bug to fix those 2 error messages. I see that the call path in Android is that nothing depends on the error code of that code path except to check against SUCCESS, so it should not be invasive.",
      "parentUuid": "dec804ac_a5762ed6",
